    "result": "Great! The issue was fixed. Here's what was happening:\n\n**The Problem:** JavaScript's floating-point arithmetic introduced precision errors when converting decimal dollars to cents. `39.95 \u00d7 100` resulted in `3995.0000000000005` instead of exactly `3995`, which failed the \"whole cents\" validation.\n\n**The Fix:** I updated three places:\n\n1. **`parseEuros()` (line 13)**: Added `Math.round()` after multiplying by 100 to clean up floating-point errors\n2. **`cellCents()` (line 25)**: Same fix for the CSV import path  \n3. **`validate()` (line 22)**: Changed the integer check from `Number.isInteger(sub.price)` to `Math.round(sub.price) !== sub.price` as a defensive measure\n\nNow 39.95 and other decimal prices work correctly without any floating-point precision issues.",
